BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Gleanwell) Tj T* () Tj T* (Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Gleanwell: Connecting Small Farms and Restaurants With Seconds Produce) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Food waste is a huge problem in the United States and around the world. Alot of this waste) Tj T* (happens at the farm level. Small farms grow produce and some of it comes out as what is called) Tj T* (seconds, meaning it is not perfect looking, it is to ripe, it is to small or to big, or it has) Tj T* (a blemish. Grocery stores and farmers markets dont want seconds so the farmers has nowhere to) Tj T* (sell them. Many small farms is also very busy and does not have time to call around to) Tj T* (restaurants or canneries to find a buyer. So the seconds produce goes to waste or gets) Tj T* (composted or left in the field. This is a loss of money for the farmer and a loss of food for) Tj T* (the world. At the same time, restaurants have rising ingredient costs and chefs are always) Tj T* (looking for lower cost ingredients especially for soups, sauces, stocks and specials where the) Tj T* (looks of the produce does not matter. Canneries and preservers also need large amounts of) Tj T* (produce at low price. So there is a problem on both sides that nobody is connecting. The farmer) Tj T* (has produce and no buyer, the chef needs produce and has no cheap source.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Gleanwell is a app that solve this problem by connecting small farms with seconds produce to) Tj T* (nearby restaurants and canneries. The farmer opens the app and posts a listing of what they) Tj T* (have, for example forty pounds of tomatoes that are very ripe, with a price and a pickup) Tj T* (window. Chefs and cannery buyers near the farm get notified and can browse listings, claim what) Tj T* (they want, and arrange pickup or delivery. Our platform is a win win for everyone. Farms earn) Tj T* (money from produce that would of been wasted, chefs get lower cost ingredients, and the) Tj T* (environment benefits from less waste. We also are building a data and analytics layer that will) Tj T* (use the listing data to help farmers predict how much surplus they will have and to price there) Tj T* (seconds better over time. We beleive this data will become a very valuable asset for the whole) Tj T* (food supply chain and gives Gleanwell a strong moat.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The market for our product is very large. There are thousands of small farms in the United) Tj T* (States and tens of thousands of restaurants and many canneries. Food waste is a multi billion) Tj T* (dollar problem. If we only capture a small percent of this market it would be a very big) Tj T* (business. Our target customers are first small farms within a short drive of a city and second) Tj T* (restaurants and canneries in that same area. We will start local in one region and then expand) Tj T* (region by region as we grow. We think the farm to restaurant trend and the growing interest in) Tj T* (sustainability and local food is a big tailwind for us. Consumers care more and more about) Tj T* (waste and chefs like to say they source local, so our app fits perfect into this trend.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our business model is a marketplace model. We plan to take a commission on each transaction) Tj T* (that happens on the platform, probably something like ten to fifteen percent, but we are still) Tj T* (figuring out the right number. We may also later charge a subscription fee for the premium) Tj T* (analytics features for farms and for restaurants who want priority access to listings. Another) Tj T* (possible revenue stream is selling the data and insights to other companies in the food) Tj T* (industry. We have not yet tested what price farmers and chefs are willing to pay so these) Tj T* (numbers is an estimate and will be validated as we get more users. Our costs include building) Tj T* (and maintaining the app, hosting, marketing to farms and restaurants, and someone to manage) Tj T* (logistics and onboarding. We believe that as the network grows the cost to acquire each new) Tj T* (user will go down because of network effects.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
