BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (The space of food waste and food marketplaces is crowded and there is many players. There are) Tj T* (other apps that sell surplus food to consumers, there are food rescue nonprofits and food banks) Tj T* (that take donations from farms, there are wholesale produce distributors and brokers, and there) Tj T* (are farm to restaurant ordering platforms. Some of these overlap with what we do. However we) Tj T* (think Gleanwell is different because we focus only on seconds produce from small farms and we) Tj T* (connect directly to restaurants and canneries, not to consumers, and because of our data and) Tj T* (analytics layer. Other competitors dont focus on small farms who is underserved. Our advantage) Tj T* (is that we is a nimble startup that is close to the local community and understand both sides) Tj T* (of the market. We know that larger players could enter our space but we think we can move) Tj T* (faster and build relationships first.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our team is three students at our university. Dalton Verhaegen is the CEO and leads business) Tj T* (development and strategy and is studying business and has worked at a restaurant and so) Tj T* (understands chef needs. Priyanka Oyelaran-Webb is the CTO and leads the app development and) Tj T* (data and she is studying computer science and has built several apps for class projects. Marcus) Tj T* (Teodorescu is responsible for operations and farm relationships and grew up around a family) Tj T* (farm and so knows the problems of small farms firsthand. Together we have the passion, the) Tj T* (skills and the vision to make Gleanwell succeed. We are very commited to this idea and willing) Tj T* (to work hard.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have reached two important milestones. First we have defined our core business) Tj T* (concept, including who our customers are and how the app would work. Second we have got our) Tj T* (first external users on the product, which are a small number of farms and a few restaurants) Tj T* (who have tried the app. We also have a website. We have not formed our legal entity yet but) Tj T* (plan to do so soon, probably as an LLC or maybe a C corp, we are still deciding. We have not) Tj T* (generated any significant revenue yet and so far the work has been paid by ourselves with our) Tj T* (own time. For the next year we expect costs for development, hosting, marketing, and a part) Tj T* (time hire for logistics. We project that in year one we will have a small number of) Tj T* (transactions, then grow quickly in year two and three as we expand to more regions and add the) Tj T* (analytics subscription. We think we could reach profitability in about three years but this) Tj T* (depend on how fast we grow the network. Our financial projections is still early and we plan to) Tj T* (refine them with the feedback from the competition and mentors.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Ask For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to this business plan competition for several reasons. First we hope to win) Tj T* (prize funding which we would use to form our legal entity, improve the app, and run a bigger) Tj T* (pilot with more farms and restaurants in our region. Second we would like mentorship from) Tj T* (experienced entrepreneurs and judges who can help us with our business model, pricing, and how) Tj T* (to scale. Third we want connections to potential investors, farm and restaurant partners, and) Tj T* (other resources in the food industry. We belive that with the right support Gleanwell can grow) Tj T* (into a major player in the food and beverage space and make a real impact on food waste while) Tj T* (helping farms and chefs. Thank you for considering our application and we look forward to the) Tj T* (opportunity to pitch to you.) Tj ET
endstream
